      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for clarifying. You mentioned these \"unanticipated elements\" and \"irregular disruptions\" that make it hard for models to predict capacity. Beyond the standard variables like pedestrians or lane changes, are there any other underlying systemic factors or psychological aspects of driver behavior that contribute to this sense of chaos or sudden, inexplicable disruption in the flow?",
